{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftml\/earlystoppingcallbacks"]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedClassifiers","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/SupervisedRegressors","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/HistogramGradientBoosting","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/ReproducibilityAndPRNG","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MLOpsExport"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Guides--Tutorials","title":"Guides & Tutorials"}],"metadata":{"title":"Early Stopping & Generalization Control","modules":[{"name":"SwiftML"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EarlyStoppingCallbacks"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EarlyStopping","doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/MetricDirection"],"title":"Training Callbacks","anchor":"Training-Callbacks"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterative estimators like multi-layer perceptrons (","type":"text"},{"code":"MLPClassifier","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MLPRegressor"},{"text":") and gradient boosted decision trees (","type":"text"},{"code":"GradientBoostedTreesRegressor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") improve their training loss over successive iterations. However, after sufficient capacity has been fit, additional epochs frequently lead to overfitting on training noise and deteriorating generalization on unseen data.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"EarlyStopping","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" provides a decoupled, value-type training callback that monitors validation loss or performance metrics across successive epochs, halting training and optionally restoring optimal model weights.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Mechanics & State Machine","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Mechanics--State-Machine"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Epoch Evaluation (Score S_t)","            │","            ▼"," Is (Best - S_t) > minDelta?","   ├── YES ──► Reset wait = 0, update bestScore = S_t, checkpoint weights","   └── NO  ──► Increment wait = wait + 1","                 │","            Is wait >= patience?","              ├── YES ──► shouldStop = true, restore best checkpoint weights","              └── NO  ──► Continue training"]},{"text":"Configuration Parameters","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Configuration-Parameters"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"patience","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": Number of consecutive non-improving evaluations tolerated before triggering an early halt."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"minDelta","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": Minimum absolute improvement required to qualify as progress.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"direction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".minimize"},{"type":"text","text":" for loss functions (cross-entropy, MSE) or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".maximize"},{"type":"text","text":" for scoring metrics (accuracy, R2, AUC)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restoreBestWeights"},{"type":"text","text":": When "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", automatically restores the model parameters from the epoch that achieved "},{"code":"bestScore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", avoiding overfit tail iterations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Example Usage","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Example-Usage"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftML","","\/\/ 1. Configure early stopping callback","let es = EarlyStopping(","    patience: 5,","    minDelta: 1e-4,","    direction: .minimize,","    restoreBestWeights: true",")","","\/\/ 2. Fit MLP with validation monitoring","let mlp = MLPClassifier(hiddenLayerSizes: [32, 16], maxIter: 200)","try await mlp.fit(","    features: X_train,","    targets: y_train,","    validationFeatures: X_val,","    validationTargets: y_val,","    earlyStopping: es",")"]}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Halt iterative training dynamically when validation performance ceases to improve to prevent overfitting."}],"references":{"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML/EnsembleLearning":{"title":"Ensemble Learning: Random Forests & Gradient Boosted Trees","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml\/ensemblelearning","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/EnsembleLearning","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Train high-accuracy bagging and boosting decision tree ensembles natively in Swift with multicore parallelism."}],"kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML/HistogramGradientBoosting":{"title":"Fast Tabular Learning with Histogram Gradient Boosting","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml\/histogramgradientboosting","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/HistogramGradientBoosting","abstract":[{"text":"Discretize continuous feature distributions into 256 compact bins to accelerate decision tree split evaluations from (O(N \\log N)) to (O(K)).","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftML/documentation/SwiftML/SupervisedClassifiers":{"title":"Supervised Classification Models","url":"\/documentation\/swiftml\/supervisedclassifiers","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftML\/documentation\/SwiftML\/Sup